  "id": "premenstrual-syndrome",
  "term": "premenstrual syndrome",
  "definition": "Premenstrual syndrome is a pattern of distressing physical, psychological, or behavioral changes that happens during the luteal phase of the menstrual cycle. Symptoms can vary widely, including pain, water retention, anxiety, cravings, and depression, and they usually lessen clearly within 2 or 3 days after menstruation begins.",
